SwiftPutty local patch 0013
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; should be (undefined behaviour)

Proxy: initialise the negotiator's reconnect flag.

proxy.h says ProxyNegotiator's standard fields are set up centrally, and
new_connection() sets done, error and aborted, but not reconnect, which
the HTTP negotiator added. The negotiators allocate with snew(), so
proxy_negotiate() read an indeterminate bool, and a nonzero byte there
made any proxy type drop its connection to the proxy and reconnect.
Found by UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer ("load of value 190, which is not a
valid value for type 'bool'") on Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c.
Applies after patch 0011.

--- a/proxy/proxy.c
+++ b/proxy/proxy.c
@@ -587,6 +587,7 @@
         ps->pn->done = false;
         ps->pn->error = NULL;
         ps->pn->aborted = false;
+        ps->pn->reconnect = false;
         ps->pn->input = &ps->pending_input_data;
         /* Provide an Interactor to the negotiator if and only if we
          * are usefully able to ask interactive questions of the user */
